<p>In 1915, Langer and S.L. Nuchols, another Mandan lawyer, formed the law firm of Langer and Nuchols. Langer was elected North Dakota Attorney General in 1916, an election in which defeated his opponent by over 58,000 votes and carried every county in the state. He was re-elected Attorney General in 1918 on the Non-Partisan League (NPL) ticket. Morton County Courthouse c. 1913 Click to Enlarge</p>

